<!--Post: 4562--><!--Time: 1106531404-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4562"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bond007<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bond007<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 5:50 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->This is a long post but interesting.  Please bear with me.  I&#39;m a Wichita native but no longer live there.  I had a conversation with a current resident and he gave me this, admittedly, hearsay, story.  I will post it hear for your evaluation. <BR> <BR>A mutual friend used to date a girl who lived on Pinecrest.  This girl said that at the time of the Anna Williams &#40;?last name&#41; incident, a neighbor had a visit from WPD.  WPD infomed her that they thought BTK had been stalking her and they strongly encouraged her to leave and stay elsewhere for an undetermined amount of time.  After some persuading, she left to stay with a friend.  After about 10 days, she got fed up with living at her friend&#39;s house and told WPD she was going to return to her house.   <BR> <BR>The WPD detective again strongly encouraged her to reconsider but she would not relent.  So, the detective had a uniformed officer meet her at the house to walk through and ensure it was undisturbed.  They found nothing.  The officer left and the woman put her daughter to bed.  As she started to look closely though, she noticed two things.  A gingerbread house her daughter had made, one that was intact when they left, was missing the rear corner.  Police would later point out that, if that were her house, the missing part was her bedroom.  The thing out of place was that the batteries in her vibrator, which was apparently very well hidden, were turned around.  She had gotten the thing out to use it and it wouldn&#39;t work.  She called the babysitter to ask if she had either damaged the gingerbread house or tampered with her vibrator.  After the babysitter assured her that she had done neither, she un-assed the area at warp speed.  Moving completely out within the month. <BR> <BR>It this story is true, then it supports what many have been saying and speculating:  that BTK has been communicating with WPD much more than we know and they are holding a lot back. <BR> <BR>What say you?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4562-->
<!--Post: 4563--><!--Time: 1106531724-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4563"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Jrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Jrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 5:55 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would agree, if true.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4563-->
<!--Post: 4571--><!--Time: 1106533463-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4571"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 6:24 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I’d like to know how they concluded that she was indeed a target.  Did BTK send some communication directly to the WPD about her?   <BR> <BR>Let’s face it, if the communication initially went directly to her house, she sounds like she would have bolted out of that house right then and there, and not wait for some other odd signals. <BR> <BR>The vibrator thing is WEIRD!!!   How would BTK even know about the vibrator?  Was he peeking through her windows perhaps?   <BR> <BR>I’ve heard that many times they get good fingerprints off batteries – so turning them around without laying prints may have his way of taunting the police? <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4571-->
<!--Post: 4579--><!--Time: 1106543336-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4579"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Denise<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Denise<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, January 23, 2005 - 9:08 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->did they even have vibrators back then? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
