<!--Post: 4586--><!--Time: 1106559311-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4586"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><a href="mailto:webmaster@catchbtk.com" target="_blank"><!--/email--><!--name-->Tom_voigt<!--/name--></b></a>
</a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Tom_voigt<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->5-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 1:35 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I have heard of this incident. Apparently the woman was sent drawings.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4586-->
<!--Post: 4592--><!--Time: 1106569163-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4592"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 4:19 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->If true, this really upsets me. Why wouldn&#39;t something like this be made known to the people of Wichita? Just one more thing to confirm all of the doubts that we, as a city, have about our LE and their concern for the residents they supposedly serve. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4592-->
<!--Post: 4595--><!--Time: 1106569801-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4595"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bond007<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bond007<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 4:30 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Tom, <BR> <BR>As recounted to me, it was the PD that was getting communications &#40;type unknown&#41; and not the woman.  She was initially skeptical.  When she asked them for proof or substantiation, the PD declined to tell her why they thought she was being stalked.  Just that they were concerned for her welfare. <BR> <BR>When they finally get this guy, it will interesting to see all the stuff we were never made privvy to.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4595-->
<!--Post: 4617--><!--Time: 1106591026-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4617"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Iceteajan<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Iceteajan<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 10:23 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I would like to know why the house itself wasn&#39;t put under surveillance &#40;whether she was in the house or not&#41; ESPECIALLY having some evidence supporting suspicion. <BR> <BR>If this is true, it means BTK got inside this house &amp; tampered with these items unbeknownst to LE?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4617-->
<!--Post: 4648--><!--Time: 1106619437-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST4648"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Cougar<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Cougar<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, January 24, 2005 - 6:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The only part of this story that rings untrue to me is how in the world would a woman ask her babysitter if she had tampered with her vibrator? I would think that would be a hard subject to address and one that might be better left alone. Asking about the gingerbread house would have been sufficient. Don&#39;t you think? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 4648-->
<!--Post: 4681--><!--Time: 1106669037-->
